hi i'm betsy and today i'm going to show  you how to make my neapolitan ice cream  cone cupcakes i love alliteration what  can i say  i did test this recipe once before i  made them i was definitely a little  nervous that the layers weren't going to  work out but they ended up working out  really well what i really love about  this recipe is that it requires mostly  store-bought ingredients  [Music]  so you have vanilla cake batter  strawberry cake batter and brownie  batter so you may be wondering why i  chose to use brownie batter instead of  just a chocolate cake batter like i did  for strawberry and vanilla well the  chocolate is going to be the base of our  layers and brownie batter tends to be  more dense than chocolate cake batter so  it'll provide that stronger base your  layers will be less likely to bleed into  each other so before filming this little  segment i actually read through some  tips that some tasty fans shared on our  website tasty.co we do read them and one  tasty fan had a really really great tip  that i think you'll find super useful so  he suggested to make your distribution  of your batters a little easier use a  piping bag and honestly i can't believe  i didn't think of that but that is a  really great tip this will also ensure  that your layers will be a little bit  more evenly distributed and less likely  to bleed into each other so you can have  those really nice  distinct layers so keep sharing your  tips because they're really good and  they're super helpful for other people  who make these recipes regularly again  it's totally fine if your layers kind of  bleed into each other a little bit i'll  personally love a great marble effect  and your cupcakes are still going to  taste really great  [Music]  so decorating these was probably my  favorite part of this recipe because in  my opinion they look like real  soft-serve ice cream cones so i decided  to use vanilla frosting for this but you  can obviously get creative with your own  favorite flavors like chocolate frosting  strawberry frosting i did use an open  star piping tip to kind of create that  soft serve effect but you can get  creative with your own piping tips that  you have at home you're still gonna have  an awesome ice cream cone at the end of  the day rainbow sprinkles are probably  my favorite thing of all time because it  just makes me really happy but what's  great about this recipe is obviously you  don't have a melty mess like running  down your fingers from ice cream it's a  different way to kind of take advantage  of those ice cream cones so after the  rainbow sprinkles obviously you gotta  put a little cherry on top to kind of  bring it all together i swear these will  probably be a huge hit at like a kid's  birthday party i know my niece and  nephew would probably go crazy over them  you could honestly eat this as if you  were eating a real ice cream cone maybe  you want to save a little bit more of  the frosting and not eat that first but  you know work your way around the cone  and have some fun with it  i guess there's no like really easy way  to eat this  [Music]  you
 

